{
  "summary": "User James O'Connor (user_id 8, Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, Chicago, usual hours 06:00-14:00) reports two issues: (1) desktop BL-DT-0108 is not on the network; (2) floor 2 printer BL-PR-FL2 is down. Checked: account active, not locked, no failed logins, VPN access enabled, sign-ins for the last 14 days all successful from corporate and residential networks. Desktop BL-DT-0108 shows online: false, last check-in 2026-10-11T01:06 UTC, no warnings, disk 78% free. Printer BL-PR-FL2 shows online: false, last check-in 2026-10-10T22:06 UTC, no warnings. Per KB-022, offline status for the printer points to the printer itself, and the printer quick checks (screen errors, power cycle, cable/link light) require someone on site. KB-014 (Wi-Fi connected but no internet) does not fit a desktop reporting no network. No KB covers a wired desktop that is offline. Needed: on-site check of desktop network connection/cable/NIC and whether the desktop is reachable remotely; on-site check of printer BL-PR-FL2 for errors, power cycle, and link light; if the printer stays offline after a power cycle, check for network or hardware fault. Possibly a wider floor 2 network or switch issue if others are also affected, which would be higher priority.",
  "reason": "Desktop is offline with no KB article covering it, and the printer is offline for all users, which needs on-site hardware checks that Tier 1 cannot perform. Escalating per KB-022 escalation guidance and the no-KB rule."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry about the rough morning. I checked your account and both devices. Your account is fine and not locked. Your desktop (BL-DT-0108) and the floor 2 printer (BL-PR-FL2) both show as offline, so this needs hands-on troubleshooting. I've passed it to our second-level team with the details. In the meantime, for the printer, please check its screen for errors like a paper jam, low paper or toner, or an open door. Then turn it off for 30 seconds and back on, and check that the network cable is plugged in and its link light is on. If you need to print right away, use another printer. For the desktop, please check that the network cable is firmly connected and note whether anyone else near you is also having network trouble, since that helps us find the cause faster. Let us know if anything changes.",
  "internal_note": "Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1). Account user_id 8 is active, not locked, 0 failed logins, VPN enabled, 14-day sign-ins all successful from corporate and residential networks, no anomalies. Desktop BL-DT-0108 is offline (last check-in 2026-10-11T01:06 UTC, no warnings, disk 78% free). Printer BL-PR-FL2 is offline for everyone (last check-in 2026-10-10T22:06 UTC). Per KB-022 this means the printer itself is the issue, so on-site checks are needed (screen errors, power cycle, cable/link light). KB-014 does not apply to a wired desktop with no network. No KB covers a wired desktop that is offline. Check whether other floor 2 devices are affected, which would point to a switch or network issue and raise priority. No actions were queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-022",
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
